the village of Bosch candy in the  foothills of the Tian Shan Mountains in  central Kyrgyzstan docked on Elima yacht  off is farmed and raised livestock all  his life it's the traditional existence  here but in recent years it's become  more difficult due to climate change is  the master we have less and less water  there's a river nearby and used to have  so much water you could barely cross it  on horseback but now the water barely  reaches the horse's belly attention it's  all semester student the mountains of  changshan are unique there are 50 500  species of plants here and many rare  animals such as the Marco Polo sheep  which are seldom seen nowadays the  glacier waters give them life but the  glaciers are receding the region's  biodiversity is in peril and life for  people here is getting more and more  difficult what can be done about it this  question led dothan al imam you drove to  a nearby village where Khanna John TF  lives with the help of environmental  organizations he's created a small oasis  here in the middle of the rocky desert  Khanna John taya grows apricots the only  fruit that can survive here this year's  harvest has already been sold it went to  Russia a good idea why waste your time  and energy on crops that won't ripen  here I could do it too sighs oh but to  come up with these ideas farmers have to  understand how to cope with changing  climate conditions help comes from  international organizations like the  German agency for international  cooperation or GI Z it trains farmers  with workshops and today a role-playing  game the farmers have to play various  parts including planners livestock  farmers and bookkeepers they're learning  how to deal with climate change instead  of watching helplessly  in a short time the farmers role play  their entire lives and suggest solutions  they're familiar with we analyzed the  most successful ones back in bosch candy  village the hope is that people here can  be better equipped for the future for a  life with climate change and not as  victims of it
 

